// The `is` COMPLEMENT over an UN-ANNOTATED (hole) parameter, at its LITERAL arm. The HIT arm
// narrows at both faces; the ELSE arm needs `U − T`, and a hole has no member list — so
// `vl check` refused `operator '*' is not defined for i32 | "err" and i32` while the
// annotated twin `function take(a: i32 | "err")` printed 10. Type-valid, clause 2.
// Found 2026-09-02 by the position-matrix harness at `argument` / `early_return_guard`.
// TWO layers, both closed: D1243 defers the remainder to the pin (`HD_GNOT`), which carries
// the `null` and `string` spellings; D1412 banks the CALL's pin for the EMITTER, whose only
// literal complement reads a union registry that softened `i32 | "err"` to `i32|string`.
// Should print 10.
function orErr(bad: boolean): i32 | "err" {
  if bad { return "err" }
  return 5
}

function take(a) {
  if a is "err" { print(0) } else { print(a * 2) }
}

take(orErr(false))
